declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-101';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 21, $j$6.1 The Thread of Promise: The Covenants$j$, $j${"readings": [{"title": "Genesis 12 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Genesis/12"}, {"title": "2 Samuel 7 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/2Samuel/7"}, {"title": "Jeremiah 31 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Jeremiah/31"}, {"title": "Luke 24 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Luke/24"}], "body": "Read Genesis 12, 2 Samuel 7, Jeremiah 31 and Luke 24 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nA covenant is a binding agreement in which God makes promises to His people. The Old Testament is built on a chain of covenants. In the garden God promised a deliverer. With Noah He promised never again to destroy the earth by a flood. With Abraham He promised a land, a nation and a blessing for all families of the earth. At Sinai He made a covenant with Israel and gave the law. With David He promised an everlasting throne. Through Jeremiah He promised a new covenant written on the heart. After His resurrection, Jesus told His disciples that the law, the prophets and the psalms all spoke of Him.\n\nKey words: covenant, promise, fulfillment, seed, blessing.\n\nYour task: (1) List four covenants from the Old Testament and one promise in each. (2) Explain how Genesis 12:3 reaches beyond Israel. (3) Tell what Jesus said about the Scriptures in Luke 24:44.\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "Welcome to the final unit of Old Testament Survey. Over five units we have walked through the Law, the history, the poetry and the prophets. Now we step back and ask one question. How does it all fit together? The answer is that one story runs through the whole Old Testament, and that story is a promise.\n\nThink of the Old Testament as a thread. At the very start, in Genesis 3:15, God promised a deliverer who would defeat the serpent. That thread is picked up again and again. Each time God makes a covenant, the thread becomes clearer.\n\nRemember what a covenant is. A covenant is a binding agreement where God commits Himself to His people. Let's trace them.\n\nGod made a covenant with Noah after the flood and promised never again to destroy the earth with water, and He set the rainbow as a sign. With Abraham, God promised a land, a great nation, and a blessing to the world. Genesis 12:3 says, and in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed. That means the promise was never meant for Israel only. At Sinai, God made a covenant with the nation of Israel and gave them the law so they would know how to live as His people.\n\nWith David, God promised in 2 Samuel 7 that his throne would be established for ever. Then through the prophets, God promised something even greater. Jeremiah 31:31 says, Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah. Verse 33 says, I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts; and will be their God, and they shall be my people.\n\nNow listen to what Jesus Christ said after He rose from the dead. He met His disciples and reminded them that everything in the Scriptures pointed to Him. Luke 24:44 says, These are the words which I spake unto you, while I was yet with you, that all things must be fulfilled, which were written in the law of Moses, and in the prophets, and in the psalms, concerning me. The Law, the Prophets and the Writings were not separate stories. They are one story, and Jesus Christ is its center.\n\nYour task is to list four covenants and a promise in each, explain how Genesis 12:3 reaches beyond Israel, and tell what Jesus said in Luke 24:44. Then take the four question check.\n\nThe Old Testament is one story, and the story is about Him. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$6.1 The Thread of Promise: The Covenants$j$);
end
$seed$;
